{"label":"1B","direction":"supports","claim":"A Taiwan public hospital's per-test price for outsourced Guardant360, a big Illumina-run liquid-biopsy test, fell 43% from 2020 to 2026, with most of the fall in the last year.","detail":"MOHW Taoyuan Hospital paid NT$144,000 per test in Jun 2020 (AA1090077; 40 tests, total NT$5.76M). In Sep 2025 it paid NT$107,000 (KA1140010; 14 tests, NT$1.498M), a 25.7% fall over about 5.25 years. In Jul 2026 it paid NT$82,000 (KA1150413; 93 tests, NT$7.626M, budget NT$9.951M). That is 23.4% below Sep 2025 and 43% below 2020 (82/144 = 0.569). Each award had a single bidder, and the winners were Kangcheng (2020), Welgene (2025) and Welgene (2026). This quantifies the earlier 'about 23% in 10 months' finding (F1108) and adds the 2020 start point. The prices are for the full test, not Illumina kits. They show how fast a high-volume Illumina-run customer's own price is deflating, and that customer's cost savings can be passed on.","url":"https://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=A.21.100.33&job_number=KA1150413","date":"2026-07-01","source_name":"Taiwan PCC procurement via openfun API","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"Adds the 2020 NT$144K baseline and the 5-year path; F1108 only had the 10-month 23% drop."},
{"label":"1C","direction":"against","claim":"The same hospital's Guardant360 contracted volume rose about 4.4x per year when the per-test price fell 23%, which shows clinical demand is price-elastic.","detail":"The Sep 2025 award covered 14 tests over 24 months, about 7 a year, at NT$107,000. The Jul 2026 award covers 93 tests over 36 months, about 31 a year, at NT$82,000 (31/7 = 4.4x). The 2020 contract was 40 tests over 24 months, about 20 a year, at NT$144,000. Volume does not move in a straight line with price, because these are hospital estimates and not actuals, and the base is tiny. Even so, falling per-test prices coincide with a much larger volume commitment. That supports the 'volume will respond to price' side and cuts against 1C and 2A, though the scale is trivial against Illumina's high-throughput Gb.","url":"https://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=A.21.100.33&job_number=KA1150413","date":"2026-07-01","source_name":"Taiwan PCC procurement via openfun API","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"F745 and F1108 cover other series; this is a new Guardant360 volume-vs-price pair."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"supports","claim":"The 2026 Guardant360 price cut at this hospital (about NT$25K per test) is far larger than the roughly $200 per test Guardant said it saves by moving to the NovaSeq X.","detail":"The price fell from NT$107,000 (Sep 2025) to NT$82,000 (Jul 2026), a cut of NT$25,000. At about NT$30–32 per US$ that is roughly $780–830 per test. The known figure for Guardant's X saving is about $200 per test (Guardant360 Liquid LDT moved to the X in May 2026). The cut is about 4x the stated saving, so the customer is competing on price or passing through more than sequencing savings. That implies pressure on suppliers, including Illumina, in the central-lab chain. This is my inference. FX is assumed, and Taiwan list prices may not follow US pricing.","url":"https://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=A.21.100.33&job_number=KA1150413","date":"2026-07-01","source_name":"Taiwan PCC procurement via openfun API","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"Compares the Taiwan price cut with the known $200 X saving, which no earlier item does."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"against","claim":"FoundationOne CDx and FoundationOne Liquid CDx were awarded at an identical NT$99,750 per test across 2023–2025, with no discounting.","detail":"FoundationOne CDx at MOHW Taoyuan was NT$1,396,500 for 14 tests in Aug 2023 (AA1120012). That is NT$99,750 by division, since the notice shows no unit price. It was NT$99,750 × 60 = NT$5,985,000 in Feb 2025 (AA1140001, winner Vita Genomics, single bid). FoundationOne Liquid CDx was NT$99,750 × 15 = NT$1,496,250 in Aug 2025 (KA1140008, Vita Genomics, single bid). FoundationOne tests run on Illumina but are priced as a captive, validated central-lab product. The flat price is a counterexample to broad deflation. Guardant360 at the same hospital fell, which suggests the pressure falls on LDT-style tests and not on FDA-approved ones.","url":"https://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=A.21.100.33&job_number=AA1140001","date":"2025-02-14","source_name":"Taiwan PCC procurement via openfun API","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"F1109 only said FoundationOne CDx was flat; this adds the Liquid CDx price and shows the flat price held across the Feb 2025 and Aug 2025 awards."},
{"label":"1C","direction":"supports","claim":"FoundationOne CDx volume contracted at Taoyuan was 60 tests for the 2025 award versus 14 tests in 2023, at the same price, which is volume growth driven by demand and not price.","detail":"Aug 2023 award: 14 tests over 24 months, about 7 a year. Feb 2025 award: 60 tests over about 36 months (Feb 2025–Feb 2028), about 20 a year (2.9x). Unit price stayed NT$99,750 in both. Liquid CDx adds 15 tests over 24 months, about 7.5 a year. This shows clinical NGS volume rising at a constant price, so cost is not the constraint. It also means the hospital's growth is a reimbursement and adoption story. Scale is tiny.","url":"https://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=A.21.100.33&job_number=AA1140001","date":"2025-02-14","source_name":"Taiwan PCC procurement via openfun API","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"New pairing of unchanged price with a 2.9x volume rise on the FoundationOne CDx line."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"supports","claim":"Welgene was awarded Taipei VGH Taoyuan's 4-item bundle (Guardant360 INFINITY) at 5.1% below budget, after the 2025 tender had to be re-run.","detail":"TY11500201 (award 11 Mar 2026): NT$3,750,000 against budget NT$3,950,000 and reserve NT$3,777,636. That is 5.1% below budget and 0.7% below the reserve. Contract period is 10 Mar 2026 to 31 Dec 2028 with one bidder. A prior notice, TY114112702 (28 Nov 2025), failed. The failed first round and the repeat at a lower reserve suggest budget reduction pressure. The bundle has no unit price, so it can't be compared with the 2025 rates.","url":"https://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=3.32.80.5&job_number=TY11500201","date":"2026-03-11","source_name":"Taiwan PCC procurement via openfun API","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"Fills the gap listed in the probe notes for TY11500201; the award total was not previously known."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"against","claim":"Guardant360 at Taichung Hospital was awarded at exactly budget (NT$1.47M, one bidder) in Dec 2025, which shows no discount at that buyer.","detail":"TH114240: award, original bid, reserve and budget are all NT$1,470,000. The method was limited tender with one bidder (Welgene), for a 1 Jan–31 Dec 2026 contract. The notice gives no unit price or test count. So this buyer shows no concession in a single-bid channel, unlike Taoyuan's 23% drop seven months later.","url":"https://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=A.21.100.36&job_number=TH114240","date":"2025-12-04","source_name":"Taiwan PCC procurement via openfun API","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"Fills a priority gap; the notice has no unit price, so it is only an at-budget datapoint."},
{"label":"1C","direction":"supports","claim":"National Taiwan University Hospital's cancer branch locked in a NT$14.25M two-year Guardant360 contract in Jan 2024, versus NT$5.7M at its Hsinchu branch in 2023, so large buyers lock in volume.","detail":"AD120120 (Jan 2024, NTUH Cancer Center branch): NT$14,250,000 for Feb 2024–Feb 2026, one bidder (Kangcheng). GD12301A (Hsinchu branch, Feb 2023): NT$5,700,000, one year, one bidder, set equal to budget. Both are lump sums, so no per-test price is available. These are one-bid, at-budget awards, so no price erosion appears in this channel, and the amounts show real clinical liquid-biopsy volume. Scale is still small against Illumina volume.","url":"https://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=A.9.51.1.9&job_number=AD120120","date":"2024-01-17","source_name":"Taiwan PCC procurement via openfun API","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"Fills two priority gaps (GD12301A and AD120120) with award totals."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"against","claim":"Guardant360 awards in 2022 at Taoyuan were at 99–99% of budget (NT$981K of NT$990K; NT$9.81M of NT$9.9M), with a single bidder each.","detail":"AA1110012 (Sep 2022): NT$981,000 vs NT$990,000 budget (−0.9%), one bidder (Kangcheng), one-year term. AA1110013 (Oct 2022): NT$9,810,000 vs NT$9,900,000 (−0.9%), three-year term, estimated quantity 1 and no unit price. Single-bid awards in 2022 show almost no price concession. The 2025–26 drop therefore came from a contract reset and not from an incremental annual concession.","url":"https://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=A.21.100.33&job_number=AA1110013","date":"2022-10-05","source_name":"Taiwan PCC procurement via openfun API","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"Fills the AA1110012 and AA1110013 gaps; no unit price is available, so the 2022 per-test price is unknown."}
